ceived_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Slice 1 of issue #7569: the serve-proxy (ID broker) typed frame codec, per the issue #5792 decision record §2.\n\n**What this lands** (`pkgs/id/src/serve_proxy.rs`, ungated pure-std module):\n- Wire format: 4-byte big-endian length prefix + typed frame (type u8, stream u32 BE, seq u64 BE, payload). The decision record fixes the types/caps, not the header layout — the v1 layout is defined and documented in the module.\n- Frame types: OPEN, DATA, CLOSE, WINDOW_UPDATE, PING, PONG, RESUME, RESUME_ACK, ERROR.\n- DATA payload cap 16 KiB enforced on encode **and** decode; oversized length prefixes are refused before the body is buffered.\n- Leg-scoped stream-ID parity (odd = initiator), scheduling classes (control frames never queue behind DATA), classified ERROR reasons (parent #5671 classes + credit-overrun / protocol-violation).\n- Credit-window primitive: 64 KiB/stream and 1 MiB/connection initial windows; `try_consume` never exceeds granted credit (invariant 5).\n\n**Tests (named oracles, per the repo testing doctrine):**\n- PBT: decode∘encode = identity over generated frames; streaming decoder chunking transparency (any byte-split yields the same frames); credit-never-exceeded over generated grant/consume sequences.\n- Unit: DATA cap boundary (16384 ok / 16385 refused both directions), truncated-frame handling, ERROR reason and WINDOW_UPDATE round-trips, stream parity.\n- Verified on the laptop: `cargo test --lib serve_proxy` — 10 passed, 0 failed.\n\n**Not in this slice** (remaining on issue #7569, in decision-record order): leg establishment (TLS 1.3 / HTTP CONNECT / WebSocket adapter), broker-side stream-ID mapping + priority scheduling across streams, keepalive/dead-leg timing (§4, fake-clock MBT), resumption state machine (§5, model-based no-duplicate/no-reorder tests), and the E2E ciphertext forwarding test.\n\nFiled by queue task 13211 (lane code-g); the task is parked on this PR's CI with the remainder named above.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796729962&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7666&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7666&signature=e89e02d27b0c1e1a9e37eba49907fcc8ed5ae00409b180d0d532a07951829c96\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7666?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-08T11:39:18Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T20:03:45Z","closed_at":"2026-11-08T20:03:43Z","merged_at":"2026-11-08T20:03:43Z","merge_commit_sha":"72377c0a3e146d509e9febf384d52b65954b048c","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gi